> Prepare balanced source pools through the native data API

The native MNIST preparation produces1000 fitting,200 validation and200 test
images, balanced across ten source classes. Source IDs prove that pools are
disjoint and respect the original train/test boundary. Labels are used only for
this preview. Pixels remain grayscale and divide by255 in Float32; there is no
threshold, crop or resize. Only D's real input maps to signed pixels2*x-1.
Noise seeds are4823(validation),4831(test),4862/4863/4864(three fit epochs) and
4877(a held-out code-change control). BatchOrder uses4847, batch size32, and
keeps the last8-row batch:32 steps per epoch,96 per optimizer.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_pools.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  const auto root = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home());
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", root);
  auto                      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(root / "saliency");
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  auto                      labels = pools[0].labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    int count = 0;
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < labels.size() && count < 2; ++k)
      if (labels[k] == c) {
        rows.push_back(k);
        ++count;
      }
  }
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), "build/dcgan_pools.png", 2, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
  std::print(
      "1000 fit /200 validation /200 test, balanced and disjoint; preview only uses labels.\n");
}
