\alttext(Three validation epochs show decreasing discriminator loss and increasing non-saturating generator loss with no early stopping.)

> Inspect all fixed-bank samples before interpreting game scores

The first40 rows of the fixed200-code test bank are shown without gallery
selection. They are weak blurry structures with checkerboard-like textures rather than clear
digit samples. Uniform interior overlap in the supplied all-one toy kernel does
not guarantee smooth samples from learned filters and a fitted model. Test D/G losses are about.252165/1.994329, and D real/fake accuracy is
1/.98. Those accuracies measure this particular adversarial game, not realistic
or diverse generation. Mean generated pixel.323393 and mean per-pixel variance
.00169251 describe output intensity/variation, not semantic coverage.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_generated.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      "build/dcgan/generated.png",
      "build/dcgan_generated.png",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("First40 fixed test codes, saved BN, no image selection.\n");
}
```
