\caption(The preserved source PNG displays unit pixels obtained from signed tanh; gray gaps are padding, not model output.)
\alttext(Forty fixed-noise generated28x28 grayscale images show weak blurry structures and textures.)

> A constant fitting mean is a useful limited baseline

The next eight panels all repeat the fitting-pool mean image. This deliberately
constant baseline has no learned distribution or diversity. Yet its coarse-pixel
MMD on the real test pool is about.000135779, compared with the GAN's.054826617.
The diagnostic averages nonoverlapping7x7 blocks into4x4 values, divides by4,
and uses the unbiased signed IMQ MMD squared. It discards fine image structure;
a constant mean can score very well. Neither a low number nor the GAN's game
accuracy establishes realistic sampling. The baseline uses fitting pixels only.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_mean.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      "build/dcgan/fit_mean.png",
      "build/dcgan_mean.png",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print(
      "Eight repeated fitting-mean images; no test pixels used to construct this baseline.\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Eight repeated fitting-mean images; no test pixels used to construct this baseline.
\image(figures/dcgan_mean.png)
// result_end
\caption(The favorable coarse statistic of this constant image demonstrates the diagnostic’s limits; it is not a competing generative model.)
\alttext(Eight identical blurred fitting-mean images form an intentionally constant coarse-pixel baseline.)

> Compare saved BN and batch BN at the same final weights

The top row below uses the saved inference moments. The bottom row uses batch
moments computed from all200 fixed test codes; the displayed first eight rows
are only a slice of that full batch. Both calls keep the checkpoint immutable.
The training path depends on the other codes in its batch, whereas saved-BN
generation is a noise-only map with source single/batch maximum error0.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_bn_paths.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore g(5003), s(0);
  auto              z = n::cast(
      n::reshape(n::models::GaussianNoise({200, 16}, 1, 4831), {200, 16}), n::DType::Float32);
  n::models::DcganGenerate(g, s, z);
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/dcgan/final.npz")) {
    if (key.rfind("0/", 0) == 0)
      g.set(key.substr(2), value);
    if (key.rfind("g_state/", 0) == 0)
      s.set(key.substr(8), value);
  }
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto saved = n::models::DcganGenerate(g, s, z), batch = n::models::DcganGenerate(g, s, z, true);
  auto images = n::concat(
      {n::slice_axis((saved.image + 1.) * .5, 0, 0, 8),
       n::slice_axis((batch.image + 1.) * .5, 0, 0, 8)},
      0);
  n::save_image_grid(images, "build/dcgan_bn_paths.png", 8, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
  n::save_npz("build/dcgan/bn_paths.npz", {{"saved", saved.image}, {"batch", batch.image}});
  std::print(
      "Full200-code bank maximum signed-pixel BN-path difference: {}\n",
      n::max(n::abs(saved.image - batch.image)).item());
}
