> Changing the code proves an active input path, not diversity quality

The first row uses the fixed test codes, the second uses seed4877, and the third
uses all-zero codes. Every generated panel uses saved BN and the same restored
weights. Different pixels establish that G is not a constant zero-latent map;
this control does not demonstrate meaningful modes or good class coverage.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_noise.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
