> Check the four first-step write owners separately

For each selected write, all other stores must remain bit exact. The next plot
shows maximum absolute changes for G weights, D weights, G saved moments and D
saved moments in the first step's four writes. Every subsequent step repeats the
ownership checks, so a shared-state mutation cannot hide behind a correct loss.
Moment captures are taken before the selected write; no moment is recomputed
using updated weights. State stores are not passed to either optimizer.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_phases.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/dcgan/phase-effects.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::vector<double> x, g, d, gs, ds;
  double              a, b, c, e;
  int                 k = 0;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    auto               tab = line.find('\t');
    std::istringstream row(line.substr(tab + 1));
    row >> a >> b >> c >> e;
    x.push_back(++k);
    g.push_back(a);
    d.push_back(b);
    gs.push_back(c);
    ds.push_back(e);
  }
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.y_limits(-.002, .15)
      .lines(x, g, "G weights", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(x, g, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .lines(x, d, "D weights", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(x, d, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .lines(x, gs, "G saved moments", {16, 145, 74}, 2)
      .points(x, gs, "", {16, 145, 74}, 4)
      .lines(x, ds, "D saved moments", {147, 51, 234}, 2)
      .points(x, ds, "", {147, 51, 234}, 4)
      .x_label("1 D moments;2 D Adam;3 G moments;4 G Adam")
      .y_label("Maximum absolute selected-store change")
      .title("Only the selected store changes at each write")
      .save_svg("build/dcgan_phases.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/dcgan_phases.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Weights and moments have different meanings; the plot checks mutation ownership, not relative parameter importance. Exact zeros identify every unselected store.)
\alttext(Four explicit first-step writes show changes in exactly one of four stores per write, with all unselected entries zero.)

> Read the coarse diagnostic alongside its baseline and the images

The final comparison below recomputes both test-pool coarse MMD values from
checkpoint outputs and fitting-pool pixels. It uses all200 test images in both
comparisons and never fits on them. The GAN's larger discrepancy, weak samples
and strong D scores are reported together; none is hidden by a gallery choice or
best-epoch selection. These small models and three epochs illustrate state and
gradient mechanics rather than establish a competitive generative benchmark.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dcgan_mmd.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto pools =
      n::models::LoadSaliency(std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency");
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> out;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/dcgan/outputs.npz"))
    out.emplace(k, v);
  auto fit = n::tile(n::mean(n::reshape(pools[0].images, {-1, 784}), {0}, true), {200, 1});
  auto x   = n::models::GanCoarsePixels(pools[2].images),
       g = n::models::GanCoarsePixels(out.at("fake")), m = n::models::GanCoarsePixels(fit);
  auto gm = n::models::ImqMmd(x, g).value.item(), mm = n::models::ImqMmd(x, m).value.item();
  std::print(
      "| Fixed final checkpoint | Coarse IMQ MMD squared |\n|---|---:|\n| DCGAN | {} |\n| Fitting "
      "mean repeated | {} |\n",
      gm,
      mm);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.y_limits(-.001, .08)
      .points({1., 2.}, {gm, mm}, "", {37, 99, 235}, 6)
      .x_label("1 DCGAN;2 repeated fitting mean")
      .y_label("Unbiased coarse-pixel IMQ MMD squared")
      .title("A constant mean exposes this metric's limited view")
      .save_svg("build/dcgan_mmd.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Fixed final checkpoint | Coarse IMQ MMD squared |
|---|---:|
| DCGAN | 0.05482661724090576 |
| Fitting mean repeated | 0.00013577938079833984 |
\image(figures/dcgan_mmd.svg)
// result_end
\caption(This statistic can be signed because it excludes within-pool diagonals. The two observed positive values are not image-quality guarantees.)
\alttext(Two coarse IMQ MMD values show the weak GAN far above an intentionally constant fitting-mean baseline.)

